<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/</link><lastBuildDate>Sat, 03 Oct 2026 17:27:52 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Americas</category><title>Tennessee prison chief who oversaw botched Christa Pike execution resigns</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261003-tennessee-prison-chief-who-oversaw-botched-christa-pike-execution-resigns</link><description>
The head of Tennessee's prison system has resigned in the first major shake-up since the stunning failed execution of Christa Pike, who is in critical condition after surviving two lethal injections. Tennessee Governor Bill Lee, who previously denied Pike clemency, has halted further executions through the rest of the year while a review is conducted.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0b87e52e-bf4c-11f1-8e0a-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26225608672619.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0b87e52e-bf4c-11f1-8e0a-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26225608672619.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e77f5a06-bf4e-11f1-ac59-ed2bb6d17f7f</guid><pubDate>Sat, 03 Oct 2026 17:24:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0b87e52e-bf4c-11f1-8e0a-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26225608672619.jpg">© Mark Humphrey, AP archives</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Flavio Bolsonaro: In the name of the father, sons, and holy ideology</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261003-flavio-bolsonaro-in-the-name-of-the-father-sons-and-holy-ideology</link><description>
The first round of Brazil’s presidential election on Sunday pits two well-known names in the political ring: Lula vs. Bolsonaro. But it’s not former president Jair Bolsonaro facing off against the incumbent head of state – it’s his eldest son, Flavio Bolsonaro. He’s less charismatic than his father but just as ideologically radical as the family patriarch.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cf0647a4-bce3-11f1-aaab-ddce071186a9/w:1024/p:16x9/flaviobolso.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cf0647a4-bce3-11f1-aaab-ddce071186a9/w:1024/p:16x9/flaviobolso.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4c5f4a8a-be5f-11f1-9cb7-435d07bfc5a0</guid><pubDate>Sat, 03 Oct 2026 09:48:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cf0647a4-bce3-11f1-aaab-ddce071186a9/w:1024/p:16x9/flaviobolso.jpg">© Amanda Perobelli, Reuters</source><dc:creator>Sébastian SEIBT</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Brazil’s Lula gears up for ‘last dance’ with run for fourth presidential term</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261002-brazil-s-lula-gears-up-for-last-dance-with-run-for-fourth-presidential-term</link><description>
President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva will stand for re-election in Brazil on Sunday. At 80, the former steelworker hopes to capitalise on his popularity and economic successes to win a fourth term in office but is neck-and-neck in the polls with far-right rival Flavio Bolsonaro.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ea92c66-b9f0-11f1-8cc7-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/WEB-IVS-NOT-26SEP-PORTADA-WEB.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ea92c66-b9f0-11f1-8cc7-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/WEB-IVS-NOT-26SEP-PORTADA-WEB.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ba316d26-be6a-11f1-a33c-cb0d77449df6</guid><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 16:20:06 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ea92c66-b9f0-11f1-8cc7-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/WEB-IVS-NOT-26SEP-PORTADA-WEB.png">© AP</source><dc:creator>Guido BURDMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Brazil: Who is presidential candidate Flavio Bolsonaro?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-brazil-who-is-presidential-candidate-flavio-bolsonaro</link><description>
He was still relatively unknown in Brazil just a few months ago. The 45-year-old senator is now neck and neck with incumbent President Lula in the polls for the upcoming presidential election. Flavio Bolsonaro's victory would add Brazil to the long list of Latin American countries that have shifted to the right or far right in recent months.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0d68ed50-be6d-11f1-a887-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-Flavio-Bolsonaro-thumb0.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0d68ed50-be6d-11f1-a887-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-Flavio-Bolsonaro-thumb0.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2f0d093c-be6d-11f1-9b4e-97a041700218</guid><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 15:06:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The 51%</category><title>The Cornell 7: Allegations spark fury over gang rape culture</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261002-the-cornell-7-allegations-spark-fury-over-gang-rape-culture</link><description>
How allegations of a gang rape at an American Ivy League university have set social media alight, sparking widespread fury over the way colleges and universities handle sexual assault cases. Also the French parliament is currently debating a major new bill aimed at tackling violence against women and children. But does it go far enough? Annette Young asks Dr Andreea Gruev-Vintila, a social psychologist who assisted with the drafting of the legislation. Plus the king of Morocco names Marrakesh mayor, Fatima Ezzahra El Mansouri, as the country's first female prime minister. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/191d2bb6-be68-11f1-90c4-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/Cornell-7.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/191d2bb6-be68-11f1-90c4-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/Cornell-7.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">54275394-be68-11f1-8e28-d5ff43d1e1a1</guid><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 14:39:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Annette YOUNG</dc:creator></item><item><category>Scoop</category><title>What the media got right and wrong about Cornell gang rape case</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/scoop/20261002-what-the-media-got-right-and-wrong-about-cornell-gang-rape-case</link><description>
The alleged gang rape at America's Cornell University has shocked many people around the world and raised questions about institutional failure and toxic masculinity. The story was first broken by student journalists and national media soon followed, thrusting it in the spotlight. While there has been excellent reporting, the story has also exposed failures in how some pieces framed officials' statements alongside Jane Doe's allegations. We take a closer look in Scoop.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2c365a72-be60-11f1-a520-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4290604926abfa920f07ce7-80944318.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2c365a72-be60-11f1-a520-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4290604926abfa920f07ce7-80944318.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2a692178-be5d-11f1-a330-a59303739563</guid><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 13:53:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>William HILDERBRANDT</dc:creator></item><item><category>Reporters</category><title>Paraguay, a tax and political haven for Brazil's far right</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261002-paraguay-a-tax-and-political-haven-for-brazil-s-far-right</link><description>
Over the past five years, applications for residence permits submitted by Brazilians in Paraguay have more than doubled. Many of them are Bolsonaro supporters who are afraid October's presidential election will be won by incumbent leader Lula – whom they accuse of plunging the Latin American giant into an unprecedented economic crisis. FRANCE 24's Fanny Lothaire, Valeria Saccone and Mélanie Blondeau report, with Jan Onoszko.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e482c62a-bd92-11f1-a98c-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/Reporters-Br%C3%A9sil.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e482c62a-bd92-11f1-a98c-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/Reporters-Br%C3%A9sil.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f1324450-bdcd-11f1-870a-59c3b8f522a3</guid><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 12:48:41 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Valeria SACCONE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>What's real and what's fake? How AI is impacting Brazil's election race</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261002-what-s-real-and-what-s-fake-how-ai-is-impacting-brazil-s-election-race</link><description>
With just two days to go before the first round of Brazil's presidential election, artificial intelligence is taking centre stage, whether it's a deepfake avatar of former president Jair Bolsonaro to support his son's candidacy, or an AI-generated working-class female voter criticising President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva. According to the Brazilian intelligence agency, disinformation will be one of the main challenges of this election. Our correspondents report.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1f8bcb24-bdb4-11f1-9627-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-IA-BRESIL-ELEX-BAIN-Lauren.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1f8bcb24-bdb4-11f1-9627-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-OOV-ECRAN-FREEZE-IA-BRESIL-ELEX-BAIN-Lauren.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">21ecd966-bdb5-11f1-a577-f1060fcd3f95</guid><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 11:34:37 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Tim VICKERY</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>Brazil's election: Lula or Bolsonaro Jr?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261002-brazil-s-election-lula-or-bolsonaro-jr</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW – Friday, October 2: We look at reactions in the French papers after high school blockades turned violent across France. We also look ahead to Brazil's two-round presidential election, which begins this weekend. The electoral campaign culminated with the cancellation of a presidential debate after both President Lula and his rival Flavio Bolsonaro pulled out. Finally, this year's Comedy Wildlife Awards finalists do not disappoint.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/17c4225e-be2e-11f1-a575-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/Anglais-2026-10-02T06-43-03-076Z.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/17c4225e-be2e-11f1-a575-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/Anglais-2026-10-02T06-43-03-076Z.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0e40373e-be26-11f1-9ce5-e527ab1a80df</guid><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 11:04:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Dheepthika LAURENT</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Lula and Bolsonaro’s mudslinging heats up ahead of weekend vote</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261002-lula-and-bolsonaro-s-mudslinging-heats-up-ahead-of-weekend-vote</link><description>
The mudslinging between Brazil’s incumbent President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva and his election rival, Flavio Bolsonaro, has heated up ahead of what is expected to be an extremely close vote this weekend. From stating loose rumours as facts, to taking comments completely out of their context, they are both doing everything they can to win a few more votes.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5e382a0a-be24-11f1-8f0b-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/80e9ca068e7c2da7a8efa6ca62c97d1c3dfa3a1a.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5e382a0a-be24-11f1-8f0b-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/80e9ca068e7c2da7a8efa6ca62c97d1c3dfa3a1a.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5eff5e72-be24-11f1-8dab-df1ba3212eed</guid><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 05:44:44 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5e382a0a-be24-11f1-8f0b-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/80e9ca068e7c2da7a8efa6ca62c97d1c3dfa3a1a.jpg">© Evaristo Sa, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tête à tête</category><title>US continues to be 'a very significant partner', UN peacekeeping chief says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261001-the-us-continue-to-be-a-very-significant-partner-un-peacekeeping-chief</link><description>
In an interview with FRANCE 24, UN peacekeeping chief Jean-Pierre Lacroix said the US continues to be "a very significant partner", despite owing $3 billion to peacekeeping. With the UN forced to cut about 25 percent of its capacity, Lacroix defended missions that cost just 0.2 percent of global military spending: "Peacekeeping is a good deal really."
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/00cfb58c-bc11-11f1-8444-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/FR-ITW-EN-TETE-A-TETE-JP-LACROIX-NO-MIX-forpt-forPT-1-OK.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/00cfb58c-bc11-11f1-8444-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/FR-ITW-EN-TETE-A-TETE-JP-LACROIX-NO-MIX-forpt-forPT-1-OK.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5a709674-bcac-11f1-8720-6f792b4816e8</guid><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 13:14:02 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marc PERELMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Convicted killer Christa Pike in ‘critical condition’ after two lethal injections fail to kill her</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261001-execution-of-convicted-us-killer-christa-pike-fails-despite-two-lethal-injections</link><description>
Christa Pike, who has been on death row in Tennessee for more than 30 years for torturing and murdering a classmate, was on Wednesday set to be executed, but the lethal injections meant to kill her failed. Pike was then transported to a medical facility, where her attorney says she remains in a "critical condition".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7a4f7cc8-bce1-11f1-a0fb-1b050e7dec5f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-30T135639Z-1416470123-RC2PTNAYXSRM-RTRMADP-3-TENNESSEE-EXECUTION.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7a4f7cc8-bce1-11f1-a0fb-1b050e7dec5f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-30T135639Z-1416470123-RC2PTNAYXSRM-RTRMADP-3-TENNESSEE-EXECUTION.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a80fd632-bd57-11f1-95bc-155fe4677766</guid><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 05:32:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7a4f7cc8-bce1-11f1-a0fb-1b050e7dec5f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-30T135639Z-1416470123-RC2PTNAYXSRM-RTRMADP-3-TENNESSEE-EXECUTION.jpg">© J. Miles Cary, USA Today Network via Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>El Salvador sets date for 2027 presidential election as Bukele seeks third term</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261001-el-salvador-sets-2027-presidential-election-as-nayib-bukele-seeks-third-term</link><description>
El Salvador will hold presidential elections on February 28, 2027, the electoral tribunal said Wednesday, opening the way for President Nayib Bukele to seek a third term after constitutional changes removed presidential term limits. Bukele has drawn praise for sharply reducing gang violence but faced criticism over rights abuses during his crackdown.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a0e6140c-bd39-11f1-9971-7be0f5469a6a/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6CE3FN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a0e6140c-bd39-11f1-9971-7be0f5469a6a/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6CE3FN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">63210db4-bd40-11f1-92fd-9bf1f1228226</guid><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 02:32:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a0e6140c-bd39-11f1-9971-7be0f5469a6a/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C6CE3FN.jpg">© Marvin Recinos, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Trump renews calls for former Federal Reserve chief Jerome Powell's resignation</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260930-trump-renews-calls-for-former-federal-reserve-chief-jerome-powell-resignation</link><description>
The Federal Reserve's watchdog on Wednesday found no grounds for a criminal referral over a roughly $1 billion cost overrun on renovations to the central bank's Washington buildings, while faulting project oversight. The findings prompted President Donald Trump to renew his call for former Fed chief Jerome Powell to resign.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/174d3e3e-bd00-11f1-a251-816a8398162d/w:1024/p:16x9/a1af0265f11cf71602d750c5f21c83ff210bf872.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/174d3e3e-bd00-11f1-a251-816a8398162d/w:1024/p:16x9/a1af0265f11cf71602d750c5f21c83ff210bf872.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e050ce5e-bd28-11f1-966b-438601146dcb</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:44:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/174d3e3e-bd00-11f1-a251-816a8398162d/w:1024/p:16x9/a1af0265f11cf71602d750c5f21c83ff210bf872.jpg">© Brendan Smialowski, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Paramount takeover of Warner Bros. Discovery clears legal hurdle</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260930-paramount-takeover-of-warner-bros-discovery-clears-legal-hurdle</link><description>
A federal judge on Wednesday approved a settlement clearing Paramount’s takeover of Warner Bros. Discovery after 12 US states challenged the deal on antitrust grounds. The agreement includes safeguards for CNN’s editorial independence and requires the merged studio to release at least 30 films a year for its first two years.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2c2a999a-bd1a-11f1-8121-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2296482973.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2c2a999a-bd1a-11f1-8121-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2296482973.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fe35c03e-bd1c-11f1-a550-530441904a9c</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:19:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2c2a999a-bd1a-11f1-8121-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2296482973.jpg">© Mario Tama, Getty Images via AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Pentagon’s Hegseth says 20 percent of US generals, admirals cut, ‘no fatties, no trannies’</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260930-pentagon-s-hegseth-says-20-pct-of-us-generals-admirals-cut-no-fatties-no-trannies</link><description>
US Defence Secretary Pete Hegseth said Wednesday that his department had cut 20 percent of US admirals, generals and officers who did not fit his vision. "Simple translation of that: no fatties, no trannies, no beardos, no weirdos, no wimps, no radicals. Just warriors – just tough, ready, committed troops," he said.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4ea1cc36-bd75-11f1-ba38-19125f84d728/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2297942896.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4ea1cc36-bd75-11f1-ba38-19125f84d728/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2297942896.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d3a3b42c-bd0b-11f1-8a4e-ab67b79dc80f</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:16:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4ea1cc36-bd75-11f1-ba38-19125f84d728/w:1024/p:16x9/063-2297942896.jpg">© Alex Wong, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Meet 'America': Trump's AI chatbot changes answers after challenging his claims</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/meet-america-trump-s-ai-chatbot-changes-answers-after-challenging-his-claims-1</link><description>
US President Donald Trump has launched "America", an AI chatbot designed as a digital portal for US government information. But its responses appear to be changing. The chatbot initially challenged several of Trump's claims, including on the 2020 election and inflation, providing evidence and links. More recently, it has refused to answer some of the same questions. Other responses still contradict Trump, while some echo his views. Vedika Bahl tests the chatbot and its varying answers in Truth or Fake.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e053cc0-bd06-11f1-b6c3-7be0f5469a6a/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-9934752996abd64a62a23a7-71615901.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e053cc0-bd06-11f1-b6c3-7be0f5469a6a/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-9934752996abd64a62a23a7-71615901.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8a1d163c-bd05-11f1-a25d-039addfcfd17</guid><pubDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:08:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>US Supreme Court clears way for Tennessee execution of woman for murder</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260930-appeals-court-halts-execution-of-tennessee-woman-less-than-two-hours-before-lethal-injection</link><description>
The US Supreme Court on Wednesday cleared the way for Tennessee to execute Christa Pike, 50, the state's first woman put to death in 200 years. The ruling came hours after a federal appeals court temporarily halted the lethal injection to consider claims that Pike's childhood sexual abuse was not adequately weighed at sentencing.
